<title>UK: UK's Schroders to stand by Clyde - paper.</title>
<headline>UK's Schroders to stand by Clyde - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gulf Canada Resources Ltd has given up hope of gaining the support of Clyde Petroleum's largest shareholder as its 500 million pound ($300 million) bid for the British oil company approaches its deadline of February 18, said the Independent newspaper.</p>
<p>Schroders, which holds 19 percent of Clyde's shares, is understood to see more value in the company than Gulf's final 120p a share offer, said the article.</p>
<p>On Wednesday fund manager PDFM confirmed it had sold its entire 16 percent stake in Clyde to the hostile bidder Gulf Canada at its offer price of 120p.</p>
</text>
